{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A miktam</b> — an esteemed psalm, like 'fine gold' (כתם פז), or a poetic term whose beginning is miktam." "<b>Protect me, El</b> — the sense is: protect me, for I have taken refuge in You; protect me, for You are YHWH; and the sense: a mighty one who is able to save me."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:19.424520845Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}